Z||000015||Cliff Pennock||08-17-2001||06:04 PM||||Not to be a jerk, but why another board that's almost exactly the same as this one? And why try recruiting people for it here? That doesn't show a lot of respect for me or the forum.<P>Is PFF not (good) enough? I had this discussion before with others and I just do not understand it.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000016||JohnF||08-17-2001||07:05 PM||||Cliff (and everyone else!),<P>There is nothing wrong with another board.  Point-and-click is here to stay.  <P>We users go to every board for info and problem solving.  PFF is great - AUS is great, too (as are others).   As with all net offerings, let the public decide if there is a difference.  <P>BTW - Cliff, I love your board!<P>For now, I will enjoy all Fiero offerings with point-and-click.||||reg||12
Z||000017||AusFiero||08-17-2001||07:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Not to be a jerk, but why another board that's almost exactly the same as this one? And why try recruiting people for it here?<P>Is PFF not (good) enough? I had this discussion before with others and I just don't understand it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your not being a jerk Cliff. I understand where you are coming from but there is plenty of people on here that have forums and chat programs about Fieros running and I have seen plenty of mentions of them here, some even as recent as the last week. I just needed some people to test it to see if it worked properly as it is free scripting. <P><B>Feel free to delete the topic now I know it works.</B> Well except the email notifications that I will work out. <P>I will also be putting a link to this forum on it anyway once the rest of my site is all worked out, as this one is the largest Fiero forum. Lots of people like myself link to it from their Fiero sites. My current Fiero page links to here and the new one I have built that is not active links to here many times.<P>PPF is great and this is where I will continue to hang out most of my time when online as I am sure others will too. Having an alternative isn't really a drama as  it will give the hardcore Fiero junkies somewhere to go if this one is down at times. <P>I am actually putting mine in place to eventually be a customer support area and a place to chuck around ideas on what things they want for their Fieros so I know whats worth developing. I put the current format in place so people wouldn't get scared away by it but actually try it out.<BR>So in essence it is going to be a forum of a different nature once it fully sorted out and tied into my shop which is nearing completion.<P>Cheers<BR>Jim<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000018||Cliff Pennock||08-17-2001||07:57 PM||||Don't get me wrong - I'm not talking as the administrator of PFF here, I'm talking as a Fiero owner. Of course people can start as many Fiero boards as they want, but that defeats the purpose, now doesn't it? By starting another board, you <B>will</B> devide the community even more. And that's my main gripe here. Again, I'm not speaking as PFF's administrator since I have <B>nothing</B> to gain or loose here because PFF is in no way a commercial enterprise.<P>When I first got my Fiero I had an incredible difficult time finding information about it. Sure, you had the email-list but receiving tons of messages in your mailbox every day was more than cumbersome. Now finally something exists where there's an abundance of information available and where thousands and thousands of Fiero owners hang out and share their knowledge. Now what will happen over time with all the new message boards? The people in the community will choose different boards for different reasons. One will like the software better, the other will choose a board because some of his friends hang out there, etc. In short, the community will get devided <B>once again</B>.<P>I don't go for the "a place for people if PFF is down" argument. PFF's uptime is near 100% and I've just increased bandwidth so it should be even faster than it already was.<P>This is incredibly difficult for me to discuss. I don't want people to get the idea that I'm trying to defend my "realm" here because I'm not. I'm just trying very hard to protect something that has taken the community years to build.||||reg||1
Z||000019||maryjane||08-17-2001||08:29 PM||||Cliff,<BR>I don't think there is much chance of this bunch splitting up, they're too close knit.<BR>We're like families everywhere, we might do some infighting, but (with a little guidance from you) we always sort things out. We speak with pride when we say we're members of PFF. Haven't seen a crew this loyal & cohesive since I left The Corps.I know what you mean about having to search for info, went thru it for years, till I found PFF. Now I can actually PLAN what I'm going to do next. Thanks for all the hard work & finances it took to get this going & keep it that way. People will visit other sites, but this is home.<BR>Don & Jane||||reg||1
Z||000020||Galen||08-17-2001||08:52 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> maybe we can get rid of those damned dirty apes?<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Ray</FONT> <FONT COLOR="gray">-</FONT> <FONT COLOR="purple"><A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks.f2.com/</A></FONT><BR>In the event I offended you, Let me state this apology. - I am incredibly sorry for my personal views, which I am granted under united states constitution to have, offended you in anyway. If you do not accept this apology. Please by all means, tell me! -||||reg||1
Z||000021||ray b||08-17-2001||09:25 PM||||clif thank you for this forum itis #1 <BR>speeds up alot now thanks for the inprovements too.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000022||AusFiero||08-17-2001||10:04 PM||||I know your not defending a realm of any kind Cliff. But a place to go when this one is down was not my main point, just a basic point none the less. When complete mine is really going to be for throwing ideas around about Fiero modifications and stuff. Now it is tested I am removing the link. Would have done earlier but was too stupid to think of it before we had power outage just after I replied to the last message. We have 70MPH winds happening at the moment and all sorts of havoc occuring so I came back soon as the conditions allowed me too.<P>As I already stated now it is tested it will change anyway to a more commercial what do people want made for Fieros site, and I will still be linking to here from my sites anyway. I think I can't really be any fairer than that.<P>I have fun here too. Hmmm on the trouble from weather thing I don't even knmow if this got through. So if it is double excuse that.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000023||AusFiero||08-17-2001||10:04 PM||||Yep, Double it was.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 08-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000024||Cheever3000||08-17-2001||10:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Of course people can start as many Fiero boards as they want, but that defeats the purpose, now doesn't it? By starting another board, you <B>will</B> devide the community even more. And that's my main gripe here.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>I understand what you're saying, Cliff, but I just disagree that it will happen.  My first thought was also "huh? why?" but Aus has already confirmed my suspicion - that it is to serve his business.  The different forums will have their own peculiarities - certain things they specialize in.  And even if other general-purpose all-encompassing forums like this one appear, the weakest link will soon fade away and be voted off.  And PFF would <B>no doubt</B> be the winner in the end.  Take a tip from American capitalism: competition is good for everybody.  Lessons will be learned from it that can benefit this forum <I>and</I> future efforts to unite and serve Fiero owners everywhere.  Archie has his forum, and I've never seen you (or him) complain.  I check it at least once a week, and if nothing else I feel better knowing it's there.  But it serves its own purpose.  I'm a member of three different Yahoo clubs now, and they each have specific reasons for their existence.  <P>More information can only be a good thing, is the way I see it.<P>You're cool, Cliff.  And you're right to question this matter.  I just think the end result will be different than you perceive.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||Archie||08-17-2001||10:12 PM||||I have to agree 100% with Cliff. <P>Aus, no offence man..... but this Forum has been a very big part of your success to this point. I believe that in the last several mmonths this Forum (with it capability to post pictures) has served you very well. <P>IMHO, it would be detrimental to your business to try to post your new ideas on the new Forum instead of right here where it all started.<P>Please excuse my spelling..... my dog (14 years old) died today and I just don't care if it's spelled right.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000026||AusFiero||08-17-2001||10:33 PM||||Sorry to hear about the dog Archie, but ummm haven't you got a forum too? What is yours used for?<BR>I just thought it would be a good idea for customer support and to chuck ideas around rather than constantly chucking them around here. Some people have accused me at stages of being here just to make money so I thought I would confine that to my own board. Afterall I only ever came here to talk Fieros and was asked by many people to start making things. Making as much as I do now was just an added bonus. My sites linking back here can only help this forum.<P>I set it up in a similar format because you really cant set a forum up any other way. Except A few changes will happen on mine to point out what it is there for. Was only testing at this stage. Yours was advertised here in the last week, not by you, granted, but I did not see such a big commotion happen then. in fact search using the words Fiero Forums on <A HREF="http://www.google.com" TARGET=_blank>www.google.com</A>  and you get 45 pages of results.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Archie||08-17-2001||10:37 PM||||Looks like everyone posted at the same time.<P>Jim, all I'm trying to say is that I think your sales & developement time will be will be hurt by trying to keep your own members informed and by trying at the same time to keep the 3000 people here informed.<P>I can see you running around like a one armed paper hanger.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000028||AusFiero||08-17-2001||10:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B><P>I can see you running around like a one armed paper hanger.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL I already am. Particularly this week as we have been battling 70 MPH winds (our neighbourhood looks like a war zone and power has been off an on) and I have been trying to see doctors while still fit in having the stage 2 scoops ready for shipping this week. So far the fine balance is working. Well till my wife took ill today. She is currently in hospital and I am about to go back up there. Suspected kidney stones or gaul stones  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>All this on only 2 to 3 hours sleep a night for the last 4 1/2 weeks. Hence the doctors a lot. Even 6 sleeping tablets cannot knock me out longer.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Archie||08-17-2001||11:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Sorry to hear about the dog Archie, but ummm haven't you got a forum too? What is yours used for?<BR> Yours was advertised here in the last week, not by you, granted, but I did not see such a big commotion happen then. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't know what my BB is used for, I haven't been there in months. I asked my web master to shut it down some time ago. <P>I'm not saying you shouldn't have one, I'm just saying that at this point you'd be doubling your work by having to post to 2 places. I belong to all the lists and forums I can find & I'll be on yours.... but you need to know that everytime I boot up this pc and go online, the 1st place I go is PFF. That's even before I check TechNet. <P>I love what you're doing and can't wait to get a bunch of your parts on my cars. But, I'd rather have you spending time on new ideas and developing the ideas you already have talked about then trying to double post everything you do.<P>I understand your reasoning and it has merit, but at this time I can only see it hindering you by doubling you work.<P>My TechNet list is not a list that was started to advertize and develope my products. At that time there was a need for a place for us older hot rodders to discuss Tech issues. From what I've seen lists and BB's that are directly related to a perticular Web Site's products are of limited success.<P>I didn't see my BB advertized. Or are you talking about TechNet? I did see someone mention TechNet but I don't remember why. I'm sure that no one has objections to mentioning other Fiero related places to get information. But, just because someone says that he saw something on such&suchFIERO.com doesn't an advertizement make.<P>Just some friendly help man, that's all I'm trying to offer.<P>Tie  things down and take care of yourself, everything else can wait.<P>BTW, can you post up some pics. of the ACTUAL Stage 2 scoops ASAP?, I'd like to see the actual parts.<P>Archie<P>PS, I'm beginning to wish I hadn't said anything.... I was just trying to point out that you were just making it harder on yourself by doing this at this time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000030||TwisT||08-18-2001||12:12 AM||||Just a note...  only my opinion...<P>I personally think Pennock's should definately remain the main forum,  as it's already well established.  But I see nothing wrong with Aus creating his own so long as it is in fact different,  both in purpose AND in content. I would no doubt participate for the sake of having a forum to go to with a different approach to chatting up Fieros...<P>Not to mention...  having another forum could really be good for us.  My brother is HEAVY into late-model Mustangs...  and there isn't just one forum,  there's a TON of 'em,  each with their own styles and purpose.  Granted,  Fieros aren't exactly as popular as Mustangs...  not nearly as many enthusiasts...  but we are extremely loyal.  I don't see quality going down as a result of "splitting" everyone up.  <P>You can't split us up...  we're Fiero owners for cryin' out loud!!!<P>Again...  just my opinion,  I could be wrong...<BR>  <P>Brett  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/italbanner3.JPG"> <P>...Website coming soon!||||reg||14
Z||000031||Songman||08-18-2001||12:32 AM||||Personally, I think any business that does business on the net should have some type of forum set up for Customer Support and Customer (and potential customer) correspondence. To me, this shows that a company is willing to respond to customers and is also willing to let customers have a public voice about their products and service. This can only serve to keep the business on it's toes.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
Z||000032||sloth85GT||08-18-2001||12:44 AM||||Here's a wild idea, it may sound stupid at first, but just hear me out. <P>Cliff, why don't you make a new topic for Aus? I'm sure that everyone here would LOVE to see that seeing as how he makes some REALLY cool stuff. I know it'd be kind of like you helping his business, but it'll also keep everyone in one forum. Less pain for everyone. <P>But if there was a new topic for Aus, then you guys should reach some kind of agreement as to what type of discussions should occur there. Like for example, keep them based on customer support and not so much advertising for new products. Unless Cliff doesn't mind that. <P>All this does is it keeps everyone in one forum and saves everyone the hassle of jumping back and forth between forums. I don't believe that in the long run PFF will lose members. PFF is THE Fiero Forum! Cliff you are the Forum GOD! That will not change, but we all have to admit, Aus is making some awesome stuff and we all want to see it. I could see there being a problem if you were both in business selling fiero parts and stuff, but you're not. Cliff isn't in it for the money, and I honestly believe Aus isn't either, he's in it because he loves Fieros and he's doing a great service to us by making the great products he is.<P>That's just my two cents.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000033||Cheever3000||08-18-2001||12:56 AM||||I don't see the need for an AusFiero section.  BTW, is he listed in the "vendors" link yet?<P>I just hope he took all my ribbin' (about only wanting to make money from us) as nothing more than wise-aker smartalec dry attempts at humor.  He seemed like someone who could laugh at jokes about himself.  I never really meant any of that.<P>We cool, Jim?<P>Wishing quick recoveries to the best of health for both you and Angie.  While I'm at it, my sympathies to Mr. Arch at the loss of his dog.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000034||AusFiero||08-18-2001||01:13 AM||||Yeah we cool Cheever. I am quite capable of taking a joke and a ribbing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> But the post above gave me a real good idea as I too do not beive I deserve or want my own section. <P>But. Cliff next to the mall how about a section called new products or vendors products so everyone like Myself, Archie, Ferarri_ Momo, Orief could showcase the wears in a separate mall basically. A new parts mall as appossed to a general mall. And how about a non Fiero related mall like I put in my test forum? I notice a few non Fiero related requests in there that would be easier to find. <P>All I intend to have in my Forum eventually is customer support and feed back and the obvious mall areas to sell stuff. I will still be pointing them back here for a general good time with a large group.<P>How about it Cliff? Can only improve things for everyone. Your own gauge panels would even be more noticeable then. <P>Also Cliff I don't know if you know this or have set up for it already but you can get paid for pointing people to Ebay. Go to <A HREF="http://www.cj.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cj.com</A>  and you can become an affiliate of Ebay as well as many other programs.  The beauty of cj is all your programs get pooled into 1 cheque.||||reg||1
Z||000035||goldiron||08-18-2001||01:31 AM||||Cliff's not on an ego trip and you have to wonder, how many forums (1-99) are needed? But there is no right answer. If I need a part or have a problem, multiple sites aren't a lot more trouble to hit than one, but certainly not as convenient.  Have to rely on inherant competitiveness and pride to keep good sites good and the rest will fade away.  Maybe its a fondness for Haarlam or that I've yet to see Aussie land, but I'll call this site home for my fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000036||grinthock||08-18-2001||01:44 AM||||Geez one comment out of me and I start sh1t storm!  <P>My final comments guys.<P>1)  Cliff you rock<P>2)  Aus you rock as well!<P>3)  This isn't for a fight, we all know that, but it had to be mentioned<P>4)  I agree with cliff, it's gonna split the group up, there are lots of people on the fiero.ORG mailing list that are NOT on pennocks!  some of those people are AMAZING fiero people too!!! I would love them to come here, I do'nt wanna see that devide.<P>5)  HEY GUYS!! Listen and READ aus's messages, it's a BETA TEST!  He is gonna use it for support and rebody ideas later.<P>6)  Nobody has brought up my discussion about mirror's and load balancing.||||reg||1
Z||000037||Galen||08-18-2001||02:13 AM||||I think your start page should be  <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/</A> .. hehe  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Everyone should make it your start page.<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000038||artherd||08-18-2001||06:44 AM||||I've got a Cisco Localdirector and plenty of servers on a fast link(In the 'states)  I'd gladly mirror pennock's, but to be honest, it's up almost 100%.  And it's fast even from halfway around the world.<P> I am subscribed to upteen fricking Fiero lists of one sort or another, the LAST thing I need is another general fiero fourm!!    <P>However, please note that's NOT what Aus is creating here, he's making a 'customer sounding board' for his buisness.  Which is not really appropriate for pennock's, but is a *great* thing for his site and an excellent way to make him accessable to all of us :)<P>Aus, I wish you the best, please see a doc about your sleeping patterns, we all want Stage2 kits!!  Oh yeah, it'd be cool to have you around for years to come too &lt;grin&gt;<P>Best!!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000039||FieroBUZZ||08-18-2001||08:19 AM||||Well, I got bit on the @ss the last time I stuck my face in a family argument, but here goes.  There seems to be quite a demand for info on modifications, both performance and appearance.  I find it hard sometimes to get exactly what I want thru search so if a new board served this area of Fierodom it would be perfect. Breakdowns of sections into wheels/tires, engine/chassis, body/interior would add a lot. I don't see any problems with splits as I regularly check lots of Fiero sites. Cliff's site rules!!!<P>Gary<BR>Just my .02<BR>"Mom, Dad's got Fiero stuff on the computer again!"||||reg||12
